  "title": "Three-fold contacts are knots on phases, and the Fano plane is their space",
  "subject": "Signed and unsigned not-all-equal on gluings whose contacts join three triangles",
  "conclusion": "At the knot angle a contact of three triangles with odd base count is a not-all-equal knot on their phases, so a gluing of such contacts is the unsigned problem on its dual, which needs seven triangles, and seven suffice. With distinct corner triangles the seven-triangle such gluings are exactly the Fano gadgets, exact for both the signed and the unsigned knot.",
